title: A switch for signals
mode: draw
chapter: Choosing
check: behaves
parts: and or not
keep: my_mux
---- intro
A **multiplexer** chooses: a select input `s` decides which of two inputs goes through to `y`. When `s` is 0, `y` is `a`; when `s` is 1, `y` is `b`. It is how a circuit picks between results.

Built from gates: "`a` while `s` is 0" is `a AND (NOT s)`, and "`b` while `s` is 1" is `b AND s`. Only one of them can be 1 at a time, so an OR joins them.
---- task
Build the multiplexer from gates: `y` follows `a` when `s` is 0, and `b` when `s` is 1.
---- start
input a 0 0
input b 0 80
input s 0 160
led y 480 60
---- answer
input a 0 0
input b 0 80
input s 0 160
not n1 120 160
and g1 240 20
and g2 240 110
or o1 360 60
led y 480 60
s -> n1.in
a -> g1.0
n1 -> g1.1
b -> g2.0
s -> g2.1
g1 -> o1.0
g2 -> o1.1
o1 -> y
---- reference
input a, b, s
led y
y = (a & ~s) | (b & s)
---- hint1
You need a NOT for `s`, two AND gates and an OR gate.
---- hint2
One AND gets `a` and NOT `s`; the other gets `b` and `s`. OR their outputs into `y`.
---- solution
`a AND (NOT s)` passes `a` while `s` is 0, `b AND s` passes `b` while `s` is 1, and the OR gives whichever one is let through.
---- done
Four gates to choose. It is kept as a chip, **my_mux**, with `s` choosing between `a` and `b`: you will build bigger switches from it.
